WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:01.829 align:start position:0%
 
we have him  no  he hasn't in every great action film  there are major stunt sequences to pull  off costumes that could spontaneously  combust and dangerous scenes performed  in freezing cold waters prey has all of  that and more in this action-packed  predator sequel  the predator costume was the cause of  some pretty major challenges for actor  dane delegro the cast talked with cinema  blend about the filming process and dane  expressed how excited he was to see the  movie because while he was filming in  the suit he couldn't see or hear  anything at all when predator's head was  facing forward dane's head was looking  down at the ground through two tiny  slits in the neck the only way he was  able to get through the fight scenes was  by following sticks on the ground and  listening to cues through a buzzing  earpiece i can't wait to see this thing  i didn't see a damn thing  number two yeah the predator suit also  went up in flames for a minute there in  the scene where raphael is trying to  hide from predator but ends up being  found and brutally eliminated dane  irritated some of the wires in his suit  while lifting his arm up to do the  slashing motion when he was walking back  to his reset mark he heard rich cohen  who talks to him through the speaker in  his ear  unfortunately he short-circuited the  battery pack right above his shoulder  doing too many takes  luckily the crew was able to get  everything off in time for him to leave  with little to no injuries number three  we've got a lot to say about the  predator suit first in discussion though  is the fact that there were six  different suits each one had their own  particular scent to it apparently that  foam latex really held onto every drop  of sweat and the scents that came along  with it after each day there'd be a team  of people wringing them out oh man they  still got the goop on you and he's like  that's not goop that's my sweat clearly  daned allegro and his suits went through  the ringer on this film there's  instances where i would squat down in my  knees and sweat would kind of shoot out  of my  zeus number four yeah no one had a good  time getting down and dirty in that  thing  the mud pit  um smelled like rotting fertilizer poo  the weird part about it is that it  actually smelled fine before they got  into it it was only after it was touched  by human flesh that it started to get  the awful smell think of a raw sewage  and then multiply that by ten and then  you have a fraction of what it's like  number five they can't catch a break  from this mud not only was it brutal  getting into the pit but it was also a  huge ordeal to clean up afterward in an  interview with bloody disgusting amber  midhunter opens up about what she went  through after leaving the pit i would  get out of that and walk over to a dark  tent with a horse trough i would stand  there and four women would hose me down  they were so sweet and lovely they gave  me hot water because it was also cold  that was a wild experience when i think  of the details  number six we're talking tons and tons  of smoke but barely anything getting  captured the crew had four machines on  the back of pickup trucks just churning  out massive amounts of smoke for the  burnt glade sequence there was so much  in fact that there were helicopters  coming out to make sure it wasn't a  brush fire the painful part of this for  dan trachtenberg was that over the  course of eight days they had to shoot  this they just couldn't get it done  because the smoke wouldn't stay in the  air at lunch i was just kind of had a  little bit of  a freak out and was like well we have to  rewrite the scene they ended up slowly  getting one shot at a time and putting  it all together but it was a longer much  more grueling process than it was  expected to be number seven we're going  back to the burnt glade sequence again  dakota beavers as a first time actor  really struggled with trying to get this  done on little to no sleep you know you  get a little  a little crazy when you haven't slept  right not only were the fans blowing  smoke in his and amber's faces as they  were trying to film but they also  couldn't hear each other and needed  earpieces  number eight dakota beavers wanted to do  as many stunts as they would let him so  badly that he didn't want anyone to know  he'd been injured because he didn't want  to be taken off the stunt when i'm  rolling in the in the dirt uh i'm not  wearing a shirt so i was just covered  with scratches there's another scene  where he's laying horizontally on the  ground and he pulled a muscle in his  abdomen pretty badly so that was  actually really painful but i didn't  tell anybody number nine there was a bit  of fear on set while filming in these  mountains around the time of the shoot  that's when all the bears were coming  out of hibernation in canada so there  needed to be a bear guard on set at all  times in case any bears approached the  set the bears were waking up and they  were hungry so we had to like kind of be  careful number 10 it was a grueling four  weeks amber midhunter and the rest of  the cast were given a mandatory boot  camp to prepare for their roles we did  weapons and we had a personal trainer  and the some people were there even with  all the training there were still plenty  of scenes that they couldn't have  imagined would be as difficult as they  are there's some level of just no  ability to prepare for some of the  things that we were doing number 11.  this seems to be a theme when it came to  the struggle of getting this movie done  amber midhunter found herself getting  completely disoriented when it came to  reshooting scenes for the sake of  getting the best flight  they'd be halfway through one scene and  then they'd tell her oh you have to go  back here oh makeup change something  something you're gonna be on the cliff i  was like what is going on because of all  these random scenes resets she  completely lost all concept of time oh  my god you're never gonna believe i'm  not gonna survive number 12 amber also  had to learn a ton of choreography for  this film she actually wishes it didn't  take as long as it did in my world i  remember that fight as a magical thing  that i learned yeah it definitely wasn't  that simple over like three days and  there was no rehearsal every free moment  she had she would get pulled into more  rehearsal to learn major fight sequences  we changed it a lot at the last minute  and you did have to learn that very  quickly in your defense number 13.  obviously there are a ton of stunts in  this film and some hard-working stunt  doubles to do them but amber like dakota  beavers wanted to do as many stunts as  they would let her she talks to slash  film about the kind of stunts she had to  perform as naaru i would learn every  stunt sequence in its entirety and as  much as i could possibly do i wanted to  do everything myself so i got to jump  off the tree i got to get thrown off of  the predator i got to fight him because  of this she even had input on how major  fight sequences would play out  dan would kind of guide the stun team  and then the stunt team would take it to  me  number 14. this was amber's most  daunting scene due to the fact it was  performed in an actual freezing cold  river though it was summertime the scene  was filmed in a glacial runoff she was  basically starting off her day with an  ice bath for five days straight though  it ended up being one of her most  rewarding scenes to pull off every day  she would just stare at the river full  of anxiety before she had to get in it  number 15. coco the shelter dog lands  the role of a lifetime as sorry naru's  fluffy sidekick yeah the dog was chaos  though everyone loved her as a companion  sometimes the set proved to be a bit  challenging for her there was a moment  during filming where producer jane myers  was trying to help everyone with their  war cry and well dog just like took off  and it had been headed for the hills the  dog trainer was not very happy with her  the doctor just looked at me he got so  mad at me that scared the dog even after  costumes being lit aflame intense boot  camps ice cold water and painful stunt  choreography this cast and crew wouldn't  have wanted prey to go any other way  what was your favorite moment from the  film

